nodecode-patsnap is a rewrite of NousResearch's NousResearch/hermes-labs-plugins:

  https://github.com/NousResearch/hermes-labs-plugins
  commit a6c7854f6fbd8ec8109199d5ded0c9c871c069d6
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Nous Research (LICENSE)

The original ships no code at all: a manifest points a harness's own MCP client
at Patsnap's hosted Streamable-HTTP server (one endpoint, one `apikey` header),
and a skill file says when to use which of the nine tools, how a search strategy
binds to its parameters, how to keep credit use down, and which mistakes to
avoid. Both are rewritten here: mcp.lisp is the small MCP client the manifest
implied (initialize, notifications/initialized, tools/list, tools/call over one
HTTP POST), tools.lisp registers the server's nine tools under a configurable
prefix and forwards every call's arguments whole, and cell.lisp carries the
skill as one manual topic plus the workflow each tool description states. The
server, its tool names, its arguments and its data are Patsnap's, unchanged.

What was left out, and why: the original's Hermes-only packaging (plugin.json,
the Desktop settings page, the profile `.env` plumbing) is replaced by the
cell's own config section, which is how a Nodecode cell declares its settings,
and the key may also come from the environment variable the section names. The
skill's advice to discover tool names with the harness's own search/describe
verbs is replaced by one extra tool, <prefix>_tools, which answers the server's
own descriptions and argument schemas. Nothing else of the original was
dropped.
